@startuml gitlab-oidc-trust

!include <awslib/AWSCommon>
!include <awslib/Compute/all>
!include <awslib/NetworkingContentDelivery/all>
!include <awslib/Storage/all>
!include <awslib/Database/all>
!include <awslib/SecurityIdentityCompliance/all>
!include <awslib/ManagementGovernance/all>
!include <awslib/General/all>
!include <awslib/Containers/all>
!include <awslib/ApplicationIntegration/all>
!include <awslib/FrontEndWebMobile/all>

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontName Helvetica
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam wrapWidth 400

skinparam sequence {
    ArrowColor #545B64
    ArrowThickness 1.5
    LifeLineBorderColor #545B64
    LifeLineBackgroundColor #F4F4F4
    ParticipantBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
    ParticipantBorderColor #232F3E
    ParticipantFontColor #232F3E
    ParticipantBorderThickness 2
    ActorBackgroundColor #FF9900
    ActorBorderColor #232F3E
    BoxBackgroundColor #F4F4F4
    BoxBorderColor #545B64
    BoxFontColor #232F3E
    DividerBackgroundColor #232F3E
    DividerBorderColor #232F3E
    DividerFontColor #FFFFFF
    GroupBackgroundColor #FFE8CC
    GroupBorderColor #FF9900
    GroupHeaderFontColor #232F3E
}

skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFF7D6
    BorderColor #E2B203
    FontColor #172B4D
}

title \n<b><size:20>Keyless AWS access: GitLab CI to AWS STS over OIDC</size></b>\n<size:12>awsplace . self-hosted GitLab at git.namanhishere.com . ap-southeast-1 . source: .gitlab-ci.yml</size>\n

box "Self-hosted GitLab (git.namanhishere.com)" #EEF1F7
    participant "GitLab CI\n(OIDC issuer)" as GitLab
    participant "job push-ecr\n.gitlab-ci.yml:345-373" as JobEcr
    participant "job publish-raftdb-image\n.gitlab-ci.yml:377-486" as JobPub
    participant "job deploy-to-aws\n.gitlab-ci.yml:501-675" as JobDeploy
end box

box "AWS account ACCOUNT_ID (ap-southeast-1)" #EAF2FB
    participant "IAM OIDC\nidentity provider" as IAM <<$IdentityandAccessManagement>>
    participant "AWS STS" as STS <<$IdentityAccessManagementAWSSTS>>
    participant "Amazon ECR\nawsplace-ecs" as ECR <<$ElasticContainerRegistry>>
end box

note over GitLab, JobDeploy #FFF7D6
  <b>No long-lived AWS credential exists anywhere in GitLab.</b>
  There is no <b>AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID</b> and no <b>AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY</b>
  in the project, group, or instance CI/CD variables.
  The only stored value is the role reference <b>${AWS_ROLE_ARN}</b>.
end note

autonumber "<b>[00]</b>"

== Token request (per job, per pipeline) ==

JobEcr -> GitLab: declare\n<b>id_tokens:</b>\n  <b>AWS_JWT_TOKEN:</b>\n    <b>aud: https://git.namanhishere.com</b>\n(.gitlab-ci.yml:356-358)
GitLab -> GitLab: mint a short-lived OIDC JWT\niss = https://git.namanhishere.com\naud = https://git.namanhishere.com\nsub = project + ref + job claims
GitLab --> JobEcr: inject <b>${AWS_JWT_TOKEN}</b> into the job environment only\n(never written to the repository, never persisted)

== Credential exchange ==

JobEcr -> STS: <b>aws sts assume-role-with-web-identity</b>\n  --role-arn <b>${AWS_ROLE_ARN}</b>\n  --role-session-name <b>"GitLabCI-${CI_PIPELINE_ID}"</b>\n  --web-identity-token <b>${AWS_JWT_TOKEN}</b>\n  --duration-seconds <b>3600</b>\n(.gitlab-ci.yml:360-367)
STS -> IAM: validate the presented JWT
IAM -> IAM: check <b>issuer</b> = the registered provider URL\ncheck <b>audience</b> (<b>aud</b>) = https://git.namanhishere.com\ncheck <b>subject</b> (<b>sub</b>) against the role trust policy condition\nverify the signature against the provider JWKS
IAM --> STS: trust decision: accept
STS --> JobEcr: <b>Credentials.[AccessKeyId, SecretAccessKey, SessionToken]</b>\nvalid for <b>3600 s</b>, then expired and unusable
JobEcr -> JobEcr: <b>export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID</b>\n<b>export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY</b>\n<b>export AWS_SESSION_TOKEN</b>\n(.gitlab-ci.yml:368-370)

note right of JobEcr #FFF7D6
  Credential lifetime is <b>3600 s</b>. It dies with the pipeline.
  Nothing to rotate, nothing to leak from a stored secret.
end note

== Registry login and use ==

JobEcr -> ECR: <b>aws ecr get-login-password</b>\n  <b>--region ${AWS_REGION}</b>\n  | <b>docker login</b>\n  <b>--username AWS</b>\n  <b>--password-stdin ${ECR_REGISTRY}</b>\n(.gitlab-ci.yml:432-433)
ECR --> JobEcr: registry session bound to the temporary credentials
JobEcr -> ECR: push the application image\n(scripts/push-ecs-image.sh, tag <b>$CI_COMMIT_SHA</b>)

== The same handshake, two more consumers ==

JobPub -> STS: identical call, distinct session name\n<b>"GitLabCI-${CI_PIPELINE_ID}-RaftDB"</b>, 3600 s\n(.gitlab-ci.yml:414-420)
note right of JobPub #FFF7D6
  This job asks for a token <b>only after</b> the credential-free
  <b>raftdb-image</b> job has built, tested and scanned the image,
  and only after it has verified the artifact identity locally.
end note
STS --> JobPub: temporary credentials, 3600 s
JobPub -> ECR: <b>docker push</b> immutable tag <b>raftdb-<sha></b>, then re-pull by digest\n(.gitlab-ci.yml:449-467)

JobDeploy -> STS: identical call, session <b>"GitLabCI-${CI_PIPELINE_ID}"</b>, 3600 s\n(.gitlab-ci.yml:549-556)
note right of JobDeploy #FFF7D6
  The digest cross-check and <b>scripts/validate-deploy-env.sh</b> run
  <b>before</b> this call (.gitlab-ci.yml:532-547), so a bad input fails
  the job before any AWS credential is ever issued.
end note
STS --> JobDeploy: temporary credentials, 3600 s

legend right
  <b>What this diagram is evidence for</b>
  Static access keys are never hard-coded, stored, or printed.
  Every AWS action in CI runs under a 3600 s STS session that
  AWS issued only after IAM verified the GitLab-signed JWT.
  Role ARN is written as ${AWS_ROLE_ARN}; the account ID is redacted.
endlegend

@enduml
